  "thumbnailAlt": "Party RSVP form beside a photo of friends celebrating a birthday with cake and party hats",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A party RSVP form is a form that collects who is coming, how many adults and children they are bringing, and any food allergies so the host can plan food, drinks and space. This template is one short page guests can answer from the invite link in under a minute. Guests who can't come can skip the headcount questions.",
    "audience": "Parents planning a kid's birthday, friends hosting a house party, and anyone throwing a milestone birthday, graduation or housewarming.",
    "useCases": [
      "A child's birthday party where you need to know which kids are coming and who has allergies",
      "A 30th, 40th or 50th birthday dinner with a fixed number of seats",
      "A housewarming where guests can bring a partner or their kids",
      "A surprise party where friends RSVP by a private link"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Use conditional logic so the headcount and food questions only appear when a guest answers Yes or Maybe.",
      "Set a closing date in Form Settings a few days before the party so you can confirm numbers with the venue or caterer.",
      "Share the form as a QR code printed on paper invites, or paste the link into your group chat."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a party RSVP form include?",
        "answer": "The guest's name, whether they are coming, how many adults and children will attend, food allergies or dietary needs, a way to reach them, and an optional message for the host. Song requests or a gift-free note are nice extras."
      },
      {
        "question": "How early should I send party RSVPs?",
        "answer": "For most birthday and house parties, send the invite two to three weeks ahead and ask guests to reply about a week before the date. That leaves time to order food and chase anyone who hasn't answered."
      },
      {
        "question": "What if a guest needs to change their RSVP?",
        "answer": "They can send a new reply, or you can edit their response yourself. Every change is kept in the response's edit history, so you can see the latest answer."
      },
      {
        "question": "Do guests need an account to RSVP?",
        "answer": "No. Guests open the link and reply without signing up. Only you need a free account to create the form and see the replies."
      }
    ]
  },
